  "description": "AMIWOK crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group P 42/m m c. Reported CIF formula moiety: 4(C6 H16 N1 1+),H12 Co1 O6 2+,C132 H282 Gd12 N12 O90 P12 6-,8(C2 H3 N1),18(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd7 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd8 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd9 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd10 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd11 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd12 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 7 components; largest component is a chain with insufficient metal sites for a 3D shape classification. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 4.553-4.626 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 128.58-132.39°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula (HNEt3)4[Co(H2O)6(H3NCH2PO3)12Gd12(O2CtBu)24(OH)6]·8MeCN·18H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies Co(II).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
